A||||14||sjp777||The V6 vs Duke war||||8||
Z||000000||sjp777||05-06-2001||02:10 AM||||I seem to be reading a lot of posts lately from duke owners whining about V6 owners dissin their 4 bangers and V6 owners posting condescending messages in regards to the duke. It almost seems like this forum is splitting into 2 factions.<P>Here's my 2 cents on the subject:<BR>2.8 owners, come down off your high horses. While the V6 may perform a little better than the duke, it's still a turd. 135hp and and an 8 second plus 0-60? It's embarrasing, especially in a GT.<P>Duke owners: Don't sweat the crys of "get a V6" You're not missing much. I don't know how many of you have actually driven the V6 version, but I wouldn't consider it something to be envious of. Neither of those motors could be remotely considered high performance and both result in the car being way underpowered. Both motors were designed for basic transportation applications<P>Let's face it, Pontiac did a lot of things right with these cars, but putting the engine in that it deserved was not one of them. They could have easily thrown the L98 in there as an option.<P>Now, before the V6 crowd starts flaming me for bagging on their turd, let me just say that I am and have been in that crowd for a decade. My current car is a perfect 88GT. It looks like it's doing 100mph when it's parked but that 2.8 is my biggest and really only disappointment with the car. I am sick and tired of riced out accords and eclipses making me look bad at stop lights. As soon as I can scrape up enough funds, that 2.8 is gettin so tossed.<P>LT1 or death<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A><p>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 05-06-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||AusFiero||05-06-2001||04:11 AM||||Here here sjp777. I totally agree with you. I own a V6 GT but think hey, so most came out with 4 cylinders, so what.<BR>From what I have seen on the net some of them iron dukes can really hoot along. In fact in this country it is probably cheaper to extract horsepower out of a duke than a V6 due to parts costs.<P>We are all Fiero owners and they deserve saving. Some of us like 4s some of us V6s and some of them lucky bastards  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> the V8s.<P>Lets keep our personal preferences to ourselves and not knock the next bloke for his preference as this is the Fiero Forum, not the V6 or Iron Duke or V8 Fiero forum.<P>They built rice burners for us to bag anyway...lol<BR> <BR> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Uaana||05-06-2001||04:12 AM||||Preach on Brother 777<BR>I have had both and the biggest advantage to having a 6.... "Sounds" meaner.. its also pretty good at beating Civics with stickers.<P>But I'll settle for a 210hp 3.4||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||05-06-2001||09:22 AM||||I must be missing something!I'm on this forum way too much and I don't recall that much bashing of one engine or another.There have been a few complaints from different members,but it did not seem to me to be a devisive subject.I personally think each owner has what they consider the best engine,model,or for that matter,make of car.And if they are feeling a need for change they will make it if possible.I have a V8 in one of my GT,s,but that in no way makes it better or worse than one that has a 4 cylinder or 6 cylinder,just different.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||05-06-2001||09:39 AM||||I'll take on an 84 accord or eclipse any day of the week. heck I whomp the pants off those 80's subaru's and toyota's all the time. guess it's all a matter of perspective. Besides if I want to whoop a new accord I'll go buy a new TA or camaro and do some mods. The point of this is the Fiero is a long dead horse, we cant possibly expect it to go against current technology and win. Tobad Pontiac did not see this cars potential to be the american version of the lamborgini or (how ever that imports name is spelled) porsh. Sorry your 6 is underpowered and I feel really bad for the duke guys self included. But you know every day I climb in that car and slip down into the seat and strap in I can't help but feeling I'm back in mommas arms as she rocks me to sleep around the 35mph turns at 55 mph, shes just  wonderfull to me. No momma dont have the muscle, She gets scared of her own shadow sometimes and shes getting older now and doesn't look the way she used to but thats ok, I love her anyway, <BR>I just come here to share my knowledge and feelings about a very special car with other people that feel the same way. Whats under the hood is the same thing thats under every hood in the world the real stuff of this car is whats under the skin. I don't take comments about my engine or paint condition personally hell I even joke about it myself but I do get mad when I hear those fieros suck or why do you like those pieces of crap. To be honest I have never heard that from anyone here. The way I see it is all of us here are related beacuse you have my mommas sister(s) sitting in your driveways. So I end my commentay with that.||||reg||12
Z||000005||firstfiero||05-06-2001||11:00 AM||||     The 4 banger owners are the one's causing the split...I've yet to see anyone starting a new thread that all 4 bangers suck!! By the way I have driven both and the 6 is a hell of alot faster. I don't have any problems with any fiero owner or what they have. If you own a fiero your one of us...end of story. I don't care if it is a perfect car or a car that's barely running you...like all of us..are trying to preserve one of the truly unique american sports cars. <BR>     By the way in my humble opinion you don't have to be fast to be a sports car. Is a spitfire,porsche 356,922,914,fiat...god I could go on and on...not a sports car becauce they don't go 0 to 60 in some crazy ass fast time? <BR>     one last point I have to be faster in my v6...I have to get to a gas station!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> one thing about the fours you can still have a ton of fiero fun and not spend have your paycheck trying to keep go juice in her. <P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">      <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||05-06-2001||11:39 AM||||There was this late nineties Camaro that was trying to race me one night. I couldn't beat him of course but shortly after that light there was a very sharp on-ramp to I-290. I went through that turn as fast as I could balancing the throttle between oversteer and understeer and when I cam out of that turn I was 100 feet ahead of that Camaro. He then blew by me at probably 100 mph on the highway. That was the best race I ever had and I don't think I could have done that in any other car with the same price tag. 0-60 times may not be there strong spot but left to right movement and you better watch out. Also I think it’s a lot harder to get a bad handling car that’s fast to handle good than it is to get a good handling car that’s slow to go fast.    <P>As for the turd thing, well, there is a solution for that, Its called the engine swap and the fiero seems to be the perfect HOT ROD car for the engine swap. It still doesn’t get the recognition it deserves. In fact the most talked about subject on this forum seems to be engine swaps. For me it’s going to be a 210 horsepower 3.4-liter v6. For others it could be the small block Chevy, 3800, SC3800, LT1, LT4, Cadillac Northstar, DOHC 3.4, OHV 3.4, Turbo 2.8/ 3.1/ 3.4, Quad four, SD4, 2.2 turbo, super high rpm 270 horsepower 2.8, and soon the mighty jap car eating LS1. You don’t have to live with that slow turd engine when you own a fiero.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||TheFiero64||05-06-2001||07:54 PM||||I like Fieros, no matter what engine they have.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||My7Fieros||05-06-2001||11:13 PM||||WTF? Sjp, if you want an LT1, go buy a Camaro, T/A, or Vette. And if you have a V6 Fiero, whats your ****ing gripe about all this supposed "4 banger bashing"? I dont have anything against 4 banger Fieros. I dont own one, and probobly never will unless I happen to come across the deal of a lifetime. None the less, get over it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||sjp777||05-06-2001||11:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>WTF? Sjp, if you want an LT1, go buy a Camaro, T/A, or Vette. And if you have a V6 Fiero, whats your ****ing gripe about all this supposed "4 banger bashing"? I dont have anything against 4 banger Fieros. I dont own one, and probobly never will unless I happen to come across the deal of a lifetime. None the less, get over it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Get bent||||reg||8
Z||000010||84Bill||05-07-2001||12:28 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>There was this late nineties Camaro that was trying to race me one night. I couldn't beat him of course but shortly after that light there was a very sharp on-ramp to I-290. I went through that turn as fast as I could balancing the throttle between oversteer and understeer and when I cam out of that turn I was 100 feet ahead of that Camaro. He then blew by me at probably 100 mph on the highway. That was the best race I ever had and I don't think I could have done that in any other car with the same price tag. 0-60 times may not be there strong spot but left to right movement and you better watch out. Also I think it’s a lot harder to get a bad handling car that’s fast to handle good than it is to get a good handling car that’s slow to go fast.    <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I spanked a Mustang one nite doing the very same thing Starting from a stoplight about 500 feet from the curve we both punched it and he started walking away when we entered a fairly hard left turn and I just kept on it and passed him. I glanced in my rear view and saw him getting smaller and he damn near wiped down the guard rail. I had the inside track thus an advantage but with a tighter turn he surely would have taken us both out and like you said it took a bit before he blew past me. I'll be willing to bet he needed a diaper change when he got home   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>I loved that curve on US1 between Vero beach and Fort Pierce and blew around there at nearly 70 every chance I could <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-07-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000011||Spektyr||05-07-2001||01:43 PM||||Hehe, my 85GT with nearly blown balljoints and bushings feels so wobbly and loose in the front I'm not sure what direction she's going to try to go when I hit the next bump, but even like that I feel confident her paws will stay planted around most moderately aggressive turns and curves.<P>My next project is to fix up the suspension a great deal, and I expect that girl to be cornering with the best of them.  In autocross, road races etc, it ain't about acceleration... it ain't about top speed.<P>It's all about <I>average</I> speed.  I don't need the brakes around town unless there's a red light.  Drop her in 2nd, let the motor wind down a bit and then just <B>turn</B>.  Use the throttle to control over/understeer, trust your tires and just nail the corner.<P>Think about it.  A 460 hemi is gonna roast a Fiero, pretty much no matter what you put in it.  But how many cars can run a hemi AND make a right hand street corner at 40mph?||||reg||1
Z||000012||StuGood||05-07-2001||10:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>...By the way I have driven both and the 6 is a hell of alot faster...I don't have any problems with any fiero owner or what they have. If you own a fiero you're one of us...end of story...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Amen to that.  BTW, I came home to Wichita this weekend (partly for a Fiero "fix"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ), and guess what... the silver GT is all took apart for repairs... the gold V6 SE's clutch is on its last leg (I mean it this time - can't stick it in 1st w/o shutting the motor off!).<P>Guess which Fiero came to my rescue?  The 1988 Duke!  Put the dash back together, gave her a couple new filters and replaced one of the broken "blackaroni" vacuum lines  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> with a flexible rubber hose, and suddenly I had wheels!  <P>BTW, if gas prices continue to rise, I might just keep on driving my Dukemobile  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     <P>||||reg||14
Z||000013||Galen||05-07-2001||11:54 PM||||I can deal with ya bashing 4bangers. but lay off My7fieros..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> arrest em  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Iron Duke Wellingsley||05-08-2001||02:49 AM||||There's no point telling other Fiero owners what to do with their cars.<P>If they post about a Duke and you think they need a V6 GT, fight the urge to tell them what they should do.  If you have heard nothing but bad things about the V6 engine, keep it to yourself.  Why?<P>That other owner is posting about a car they cherish; a loved one in many cases.<P>If I said "You need to give your wife the attitude adjustment . . ." You would react negatively to me.  If I said "The only thing to do with a dog like yours is to shoot it and get another one" then you would react negatively to me.<P>So, why is it any surprise when someone says "the only good thing to do with a Duke Fiero is swap the engine . . ."  There is a negative reaction.  It's really not any different.<P>Let's say a Duke owner is 30 hours into an engine rebuild, posting for help, and you respond with "the only good thing to do with an Iron Puke is to sell it and buy a GT . . ."   By the same principle, they may react negatively.<P>Since I have purchased my Fiero, I cannot count the number of times people have given me the same tired advice "swap to a V6"  It actually makes me mad now.<P>I do not want to!<P>Why?  It's $2.25 a gallon for gas now.  While my Duke Fiero is in car surgery, I have been driving my 1994 Ford Ranger at a pathetic 18 MPG.  That works out to $400 per month in gas.  $400!<P>If I can get better than 25 MPG out of a freshly rebuilt Duke (got that before the rebuild) I save at least $100 every month.<P>That I feel in love with the 1984 2M4 Fiero in 1983 just adds to my desire to have an Iron Duke Fiero.  <P>I am not saying V6 cars are any less desireable, I just never dreamed of owning one.  Maybe it's the GT fastback body.  Maybe it's the aero nose.  <P>Really, I think it's the 2M4 nose and the black bumperettes that do it for me.  Maybe it's just the memories of a daydreaming teenager that did come true.  <P>I have a collection of 1984 CDs that I keep in my car: Genesis "Genesis", Concrete Blonde "Still in Hollywood", Frankie Goes to Hollywood "Pleaseuredome", The Cult "Dreamtime", The Cars "Heartbeat City", Van Halen "1984", and so on.    <P>Whatever the case, I want a Forum that respects me for loving and caring for my car, Duke or V6.  I want answers to the questions I post, not to be redirected into an engine swap I don't want.<P>It's your Forum, how do you want to be treated?  Set a better example and we will all benefit from it.<P>All Fieros are great.  I notice ALL of them as I try to keep hope commuting in my stupid pickup truck.  I see the Yellow Formula.  I see the grey 2M4.  I see the white 2M6.  They are all part of my daily routine.<P>I wonder if anyone misses my white 84 2M4?  <P>All I know is that there is life without the Forum.  Life without the Fiero is **** !<P>Give the Duke guys a chance to brag.  And let the V6 guys modify their engines as they see fit.  This Forum is big enough for all the lucky ones that saw through the bull ****  and bought one of the best cars ever made.<P>Fastest Piston engine car?  <P>Definitely not a Fiero, Olds 4 cylinder Quad 4 concept vehicle I think.  Then there's the Maclaren F1 . . . only $1 million dollars if you can find one.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Iron Duke Wellingsley (edited 05-08-2001).]||||reg||6
